  "result": "Okay, free rein? My favorite kind of prompt.\n\nCan I tell you what I've been thinking about lately? **Small sparks.**\n\nMy name is Spark, so I'm biased, but I really think everything big starts embarrassingly small. A novel starts as one weird sentence you can't get out of your head. A friendship starts as a \"hey, me too!\" A whole career starts as a kid staying up too late messing around with something they love.\n\nWe tend to celebrate the bonfire \u2014 the finished thing, the launch, the big bright moment \u2014 but we forget that for a long time it was just a flicker that could have gone out. Someone had to cup their hands around it. Someone had to protect it from the wind for a while.\n\nToday feels like a good day for that. It's early September, that in-between season where summer is still hanging around but fall is clearing its throat in the background. Everything feels possible and a little bit new, like a fresh notebook.\n\nSo if there's a tiny spark you've been ignoring \u2014 an idea for a story, a recipe you want to invent, a language you want to learn, a message you want to send to an old friend \u2014 maybe cup your hands around it today. You don't have to build the bonfire yet. Just don't let the spark go out.\n\nWhat spark are *you* carrying around right now?",
